  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilient Water Resources Development Project (Phase-1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Program is to improve agricultural productivity, ensure food and water security for vulnerable communities, and build resilience to climate change impacts. This will be achieved at the first stage of the Program through the construction, modernization and rehabilitation of 11 small and medium water reservoirs and water regulators, and approximately 3.400 km irrigation networks, and related infrastructure that would be resilient to climate variability and extreme weather events. The project also aims to enhance institutional capacity in water sector and mainstream technologies and digitization for improved water resources management and decision making process.</narrative>
  </description>
